<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of the Iberians</h1><p class="st-meta">888 CE – 1008 CE · capital Artanuji</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The kingdom of the Georgian Bagratids in Tao-Klarjeti, a land of great monasteries whose rulers prepared the unification of Georgia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Early in the 9th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrationi-dynasty">Bagratid</a> prince Ashot I moved from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-iberia">Kartli</a> to the south-western borderland of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klarjeti">Klarjeti</a>, where he rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artanuji">Artanuji</a> and the family won Byzantine titles. In 888 his descendant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adarnase-iv-of-iberia">Adarnase IV</a> took the title king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberians">Iberians</a>, restoring the royal title in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/georgia">Georgia</a> after three centuries.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Several <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrationi-dynasty">Bagratid</a> branches shared rule over Tao, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klarjeti">Klarjeti</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shavsheti">Shavsheti</a>, with titles granted by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>. Monks led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grigol-of-khandzta">Grigol of Khandzta</a> founded monasteries, and great churches rose at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oshki">Oshki</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishkhani">Ishkhani</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khakhuli-monastery">Khakhuli</a>, centres of Georgian learning. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-iii-kuropalates">David III Kouropalates</a> of Tao made the region powerful and helped <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> against the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bardas-skleros">Bardas Skleros</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> III died in 1000, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a> annexed his lands of Tao to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>. The remaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrationi-dynasty">Bagratid</a> holdings passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrat-iii-of-georgia">Bagrat III</a>, who in 1008 united them with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-abkhazia">Abkhazia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-iberia">Kartli</a> in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-georgia">Kingdom of Georgia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-the-iberians.jpg" alt="Kingdom of the Iberians" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Ec.Domnowall (vectorisation SVG) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kartli_-_drosha_jvari.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>888 CE – 1008 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Artanuji</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Adarnase IV, David III Kouropalates, Gurgen</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Georgian Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Georgian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>, <a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tao-Klarjeti, Kingdom of Tao-Klarjeti, Kouropalatate of Iberia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=948&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-iberians" aria-label="Kingdom of the Iberians on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5708 710 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of the Iberians lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6028 966L6091 947M6028 966L5709 970M6028 966L6036 930"/><path class="map-dot-